      "body": "## Motivation\nAdd CPU coverage for `DefaultModelLoader`'s loader-specific extra-config validation so typos and format-incompatible options fail instead of being silently accepted.\n\nCloses #47607\n\n## Modifications\n- Verify unknown keys such as `num_thread` are rejected.\n- Verify `enable_gds` is rejected for `SAFETENSORS` and accepted for `FASTSAFETENSORS`.\n- The invalid `enable_gds` type case is already covered by `test_fastsafetensors_enable_gds_requires_boolean` in `test_prefetch_checkpoints.py`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\nNot applicable; this is a CPU unit-test-only change and does not affect model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\nNot applicable; this test-only change does not affect inference speed.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41175307351](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41175307351)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41175307433](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41175307433)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41175307322](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41175307322)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
